TITLE:: StepButton
summary:: Increment/decrement arrows for stepping.
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMLib, Classes/View

DESCRIPTION::
Increment/decrement arrows for stepping values. Simply attach it to any View which has value and valueAction using "target",
or use a custom Action for the stepper. A customizeable meta key increases the step.
Gets the ControlSpec step automatically, if it is present ( and not zero).


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

ARGUMENT:: parent

ARGUMENT:: bounds

ARGUMENT:: target
The target View (must accept value and valueAction);


ARGUMENT:: incrColor

ARGUMENT:: decrColor

ARGUMENT:: horz
default: true  for horizontal arrows

ARGUMENT:: eq
default: true use equilateral triangles

ARGUMENT:: inset
inset the icon by a Point(x,y)


METHOD:: newHorz
convenience method for horz=true

METHOD:: newFill
convenience method for eq=false

METHOD:: newHorzFill
convenience method for horz=true, eq=false


METHOD:: defaultIncrColor
METHOD:: defaultDecrColor

PRIVATE:: initClass



INSTANCEMETHODS::

PRIVATE:: mouseDown

PRIVATE:: init

METHOD:: target
the targeted input view. The target View (must accept value and valueAction);

METHOD:: step
default 1
METHOD:: bigStep
default 5


METHOD:: gap
default 0.5. The gap between the arrows.


METHOD:: customAction
a custom action instead of calling valueAction on the target.
code::
{|step| step.postln}
::


PRIVATE:: prDoAction



PRIVATE:: drawRect

PRIVATE:: drawWidget



METHOD:: modifier
default 524288. Set the modifier for the bigStep


PRIVATE:: mouseUp



EXAMPLES::

code::
(
w=FlowView.new.flow{|w|
	b=NumberBox(w,40@27).value_(1);
	StepButton(w,27@27,target:b);
	w.startRow;

	c=EZSlider(w,300@27,"demo", [0,10,'linear',0.1]).value_(0);
	// gets the ControlSpec step automatically, if it is present ( and not zero)
	StepButton(w,27@27,target:c,horz:true);
	w.startRow;
	q=StepButton(w,27@27);
	b=NumberBox(w,40@27).value_(1);
	q.target=b;
	w.startRow;
	q=StepButton(w,27@27, inset: 5@5);
	b=NumberBox(w,40@27).value_(1);
	q.target=b;
	w.startRow;

	// fill the rect
	b=NumberBox(w,40@27).value_(1);
	StepButton(w,27@27,target:b,eq:false);
	w.startRow;

	// inset the icon, and no eq
	c=EZSlider(w,300@27,"demo", [0,10,'linear',0.1]).value_(0);
	StepButton(w,27@27,target:c,horz:true,eq:false, inset: 5@5);


	// use a larger gap
	c=EZSlider(w,300@27,"demo", [0,10,'linear',0.1]).value_(0);
    StepButton(w,50@27,target:c,horz:true,eq:false).gap_(5);

}
);

::
